{
  "title": "Modified function stockOf to subtract held stock",
  "context": [
    "Stock that is held for another order still counted as available, so a shopper could reserve units that were already promised. A reservation now succeeds only for the units that nobody holds.",
    "",
    "## Overview",
    "",
    "- **When** a shopper reserves 11 units of `tea-01`, with 12 in stock and 2 held, **then** [the reservation returns `null`](code:src/checkout/reserve.ts#L9). It returned a reservation before.",
    "- **When** a shopper reserves 10 units of `tea-01`, **then** nothing changes.",
    "- **When** a shopper reserves a product that has no held units, such as `mug-07`, **then** nothing changes.",
    "",
    "## Implementation",
    "",
    "**`src/inventory/stock.ts`**",
    "",
    "- Added [`heldBySku`](code:src/inventory/stock.ts#heldBySku), a record of the units held per SKU, with 2 units held of `tea-01`.",
    "- Modified [`stockOf()`](code:src/inventory/stock.ts#stockOf) to return the stock of a SKU minus the units held of that SKU."
  ],
  "diff": [
    "diff --git a/src/inventory/stock.ts b/src/inventory/stock.ts",
    "--- a/src/inventory/stock.ts",
    "+++ b/src/inventory/stock.ts",
    "@@ -1,0 +2 @@",
    "+const heldBySku: Record<string, number> = { \"tea-01\": 2 };",
    "@@ -4 +5 @@",
    "-  return stockBySku[sku] ?? 0;",
    "+  return (stockBySku[sku] ?? 0) - (heldBySku[sku] ?? 0);"
  ],
